course: dictionary
lesson: 14383
title: Finding your way with oriented
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Oriented means pointed or turned in a certain direction. «The map was oriented north, so the top of the page pointed to the north.» The map is turned so its north matches the real north. That is what oriented means here.
explain: If you oriented yourself, you worked out where you are and which way to go. «When the lights went out, Sam oriented himself by the window and found the door.» He used what he could see to work out his direction.
explain: The ending -oriented, as in family-oriented or goal-oriented, means mainly aimed at or interested in something. «The park is family-oriented, so it has a playground for little children.» The park is made mainly for families.
fact: «Oriented» means pointed or turned in a certain direction.
fact: If you «get oriented», you find out where you are and which way to go.
fact: In maths, a shape that is oriented differently has been turned or rotated.
fact: «Child-oriented» means made mainly for children.
fact: «Oriented» can also be spelled «orientated», which is the usual spelling in the UK.
exercise: «When Sam woke in the dark, he oriented himself by the window.» What did Sam do? | He painted the window | He fell asleep again | He turned off the light | *He worked out where he was and which way to go
exercise: In maths, what does it mean if a shape is oriented differently? | It has been counted | It has been made smaller | *It has been turned or rotated | It has been coloured in
exercise: «The new game is goal-oriented, so every level has a clear target.» What does goal-oriented mean? | Only for grown-ups | Very noisy and loud | Full of games with no goals at all | *Mainly aimed at reaching goals
test: «The arrow on the compass was oriented towards north.» What does oriented mean here? | Painted bright red | Broken into pieces | *Pointed in a certain direction | Hidden under a cloth
test: «The club is child-oriented, so its activities are made for children.» What does child-oriented mean? | *Mainly made for children | Only open at night | Mainly for grown-ups | Free for everyone to stop at any time
exam: Which phrase means to find out where you are and which way to go? | Get dressed | *Get oriented | Get tired | Get bored
